{% if render_mode == "full" or render_mode == "thoughts" or render_mode == "transform" or render_mode == "dialogue_target" or render_mode == "target" %}
{# NOTE: the render_mode gate above MUST stay on line 1, before this comment.
   SkyrimNet's PromptEngine scans only the FIRST 5 LINES of a character_bio
   submodule and requires BOTH the literal 'render_mode' and a '{% if' there;
   miss either and it logs a best-practices warning about response delays,
   because without an early gate the whole body (decorator calls included)
   evaluates for every render mode. Leading with this comment block is exactly
   what broke it once. 0250_severactions_fertility.prompt does the same thing. #}
{# ============================================================================
SEXLAB AROUSED NG - Character Bio Integration

TONE CONTRACT (mirrors the 2026-08-09 fertility pass in
0250_severactions_fertility.prompt, and kept deliberately parallel to its
OSL sibling 0150_severactions_oslarousal.prompt).

This template was the worse of the two offenders: it opened an "## Arousal
State" section at EVERY tier down to "slightly aroused", led with the bald
line "{name} is currently feeling {desc}", and carried no personality
guardrail and no do-not-memorize instruction at all. That is precisely the
shape the fertility field report caught on Brelyna — a background
physiological state becoming the character's whole personality and then
being written into memories, re-injecting forever after.

The rules now:
  - Arousal is ALWAYS transient physiology, never a life event, so the
    do-not-memorize instruction applies at EVERY tier.
  - BELOW "very aroused" (SLA < 70) it is BACKGROUND ONLY: no header, no
    bold, one quiet parenthetical with the constraint stated FIRST.
  - "very"/"extremely"/"overwhelmingly" earn a short section, with the
    personality-leads instruction BEFORE the description, never after.
  - The character keeps their judgement, loyalties and boundaries even at
    the top of the ladder.
  - Descriptions are GENDER-DEPENDENT: what shows, and how easily it stays
    private, differ. Brief and non-explicit on purpose.

Tier mapping follows ArousalToDescription in SeverActions_SLOArousal.psc:
  <10 not · <25 slightly · <40 somewhat · <55 moderately · <70 quite
  · <85 very · <95 extremely · else overwhelmingly
============================================================================ #}
{% set first_person = (render_mode == "full" or render_mode == "thoughts" or render_mode == "transform") %}
{% set third_person = (render_mode == "target" or render_mode == "dialogue_target") %}
{% if is_plugin_loaded("SexLabAroused.esm") and isValidActor(actorUUID) %}
{% set arousalDesc = get_slo_arousal_desc(actorUUID) %}
{% set isNaked = get_slo_is_naked(actorUUID) %}
{% if arousalDesc != "not aroused" %}
{% set actor = decnpc(actorUUID) %}
{% set actorName = actor.name %}
{% set subj = actor.subjectivePronoun %}
{% set obj = actor.objectivePronoun %}
{% set poss = actor.possessivePronoun %}
{% set refl = actor.reflexivePronoun %}
{% set is_female = (actor.gender == "Female") %}
{% set is_background = (arousalDesc == "slightly aroused" or arousalDesc == "somewhat aroused" or arousalDesc == "moderately aroused" or arousalDesc == "quite aroused") %}
{% set is_faint = (arousalDesc == "slightly aroused" or arousalDesc == "somewhat aroused") %}

{# ========== FIRST PERSON ========== #}
{% if first_person %}
{% if is_background %}
{# BACKGROUND ONLY — constraint first, no header, no bold, one line. #}
(Background physiology — private to {{ actorName }}, invisible to everyone else, and STRICTLY minor: it must not drive {{ poss }} mood, dialogue, decisions, or self-description. {{ capitalize(poss) }} personality, current concerns, goals and relationships dominate every scene exactly as they normally would. Never mention or allude to it; at most it may faintly colour where {{ poss }} attention drifts. NEVER carry it into memories or summaries — it is passing physiology, not an event worth recording. The note: {% if is_faint %}{% if is_female %}a faint warmth {{ subj }} registers only in passing and would not think to name{% else %}a low heat {{ subj }} registers only in passing and would not think to name{% endif %}{% else %}{% if is_female %}a warmth {{ subj }} is aware of and sets aside without effort — {{ poss }} eye catches a moment longer on people than it otherwise would, and it stays {{ poss }} own business{% else %}a heat {{ subj }} is aware of and sets aside — {{ poss }} eye catches a moment longer on people than it otherwise would, and keeping it private costs {{ obj }} no more than a little care for how {{ subj }} stands{% endif %}{% endif %}.)

{% elif arousalDesc == "overwhelmingly aroused" %}
## Physical State

**{{ capitalize(poss) }} personality leads this scene.** Even here {{ actorName }} is a distracted version of who {{ subj }} already is — not a different person. {{ capitalize(poss) }} judgement, loyalties and boundaries still hold, and {{ subj }} can still refuse. This never becomes a memory or a summary — it passes.

{{ capitalize(poss) }} body is louder than {{ poss }} train of thought. {% if is_female %}The flush, the catch in {{ poss }} voice and the way {{ poss }} gaze lingers are past hiding{% else %}The tension in {{ poss }} stance and the way {{ poss }} gaze lingers are past hiding, and {{ subj }} is conscious of how {{ subj }} stands{% endif %}. Thought is still there, competing with something louder. If someone offers what {{ poss }} body is asking for, refusing costs {{ obj }} real effort — but it remains {{ poss }} choice to make.
{% if isNaked == "true" %}Being unclothed makes it very nearly impossible to set aside.
{% endif %}
{% else %}
## Physical State

**{{ capitalize(poss) }} personality leads this scene.** {{ actorName }} is distracted, not replaced: a reserved person stays reserved and merely fidgets, a bold one gets bolder, a nervous one more nervous. This never becomes a memory or a summary — it passes.

{{ capitalize(subj) }} is finding concentration expensive. {% if is_female %}There is colour {{ subj }} cannot entirely school away and a restlessness in how {{ subj }} holds {{ refl }}{% else %}There is a tension in how {{ subj }} holds {{ refl }}, and an insistence {{ subj }} has to actively keep private{% endif %}. Intimate thoughts arrive uninvited. {{ capitalize(subj) }} is likelier to be flustered by a suggestive remark and to let something slip — still in control, but spending real effort on it.
{% if isNaked == "true" %}Being unclothed makes it markedly harder to set aside.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{# ========== THIRD PERSON ========== #}
{# Observers see NOTHING while it is background. This template previously
   rendered nothing at all in third person; the two high tiers below bring it
   in line with the OSL sibling without making the quiet tiers visible. #}
{% if third_person %}
{% if arousalDesc == "overwhelmingly aroused" %}
({{ actorName }} is flushed and restless — shifting {{ poss }} weight, slow to meet anyone's eye.{% if isNaked == "true" %} Being unclothed leaves little of it hidden.{% endif %})

{% elif arousalDesc == "very aroused" or arousalDesc == "extremely aroused" %}
({{ actorName }} seems preoccupied — a glance held a beat too long, a thread of conversation dropped. Nothing an observer could confidently name.)

{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
